sequenceDiagram
    %% ensureService (ts/src/service/client.ts) and startService (service.ts)
    participant door as Front door (archer mcp or CLI)
    participant client as service client
    participant svc as archer serve (detached)
    participant acct as Account state dir
    participant proj as Project checkout
    door->>client: present_diagram, attach_project or start_service
    client->>svc: connect archer.sock, hello
    alt a service already answers
        svc-->>client: protocolVersion, version, homeUrl
    else nothing listening and auto-start allowed
        client->>svc: spawn node archer.js serve --foreground, detached, log to service.log
        activate svc
        svc->>acct: take archer.lock, read service.json (token, port)
        svc->>svc: bind explicit/configured port or remembered port with free-port fallback
        svc->>acct: write service.json, new token if the port changed
        loop each project marked attached in runtime/index.json
            svc->>acct: read runtime recovery record and source blobs
            svc->>proj: recompile and start a watcher
        end
        client->>svc: hello, retried every 50 ms for up to 15 s
        svc-->>client: protocolVersion, version, homeUrl
    end
    client->>svc: attach root
    svc->>proj: findProject, ProjectState.open, reload
    svc->>acct: persist record, mark attached
    svc-->>client: root, name, url .../token/p/slug/
    client-->>door: the project page URL
    Note over svc: One service per user serves up to 64 projects
    door->>client: stop_service
    client->>svc: stop
    svc-->>client: stopping
    deactivate svc
